  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Finance for Development - Illicit Finance (Regional) - ODA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This World Bank initiative aims to help Western Balkan economies reduce informality in their economies, with a view to tackling illicit finance. It will support their efforts to reduce their reliance on cash, and expand the use of secure, affordable, and inclusive digital financial services. While recent reforms have modernised payment systems and aligned legal frameworks with European standards, everyday usage of digital payments remains low. The project will focus on changing behaviours and building trust in digital finance through practical incentives, targeted financial education, and improved remittance practices. It will support the formalisation of remittance flows, promote user-friendly digital products, and deliver locally tailored education on topics such as fraud prevention and managing digital accounts. By combining evidence-based interventions with regional cooperation and peer learning, the program seeks to create a more transparent and resilient financial ecosystem that benefits households, businesses, and governments alike, ultimately fostering economic integration and inclusive growth across the Western Balkans.</narrative>
  </description>
